UPDATE public.showcase_items
SET content = E'What is vibe coding?\nVibe coding is the practice of building software by describing intent in natural language and letting an AI partner draft, refactor and ship the code. You stay in the driver seat: setting direction, reviewing diffs, owning the architecture. The AI handles the keystrokes.\n\nThe term was coined by Andrej Karpathy in February 2025 and spread quickly as tools like Lovable, Cursor and Claude Code made it realistic to assemble production apps from a series of conversations instead of line-by-line typing.\n\nWhy builders care\nSpeed. A weekend prototype now ships in an evening. A landing page in minutes.\nLower friction. Designers, founders and operators can ship working software without a full engineering hire.\nTighter loops. Idea, build, test, learn, compressed into a single sitting.\n\nHow it fits a professional pipeline\nVibe coding does not replace engineering rigour. It changes where the rigour lives.\n\n1. Intent first.\nWrite a clear brief. The clearer the prompt, the cleaner the diff.\n\n2. Small steps.\nShip one capability at a time. Review every change.\n\n3. Tests and types.\nKeep the safety net the AI can lean on.\n\n4. Human review at the seams.\nAuth, payments, data models, anything user-facing, read the code.\n\n5. Observability.\nLogs, errors, analytics. Know what shipped is actually doing.\n\nWhere the collective comes in\n<Good Vibes Café/> is a collective of builders, strategists and connectors who vibe code in the open. We share what worked, what broke, and the playbooks behind it.\n\nBrowse the Showcase for case studies, tools and sample code from members.\nDrop into the Forum to ask, swap prompts and find collaborators.\nJoin an Event to pair up on a build or watch a teardown live.\n\nStart vibing\n1. Pick one small problem worth solving.\n2. Open your AI builder and describe the first slice.\n3. Ship it. Share it in the Forum. Iterate.\n\nThat is the whole loop. Welcome to the café.\n\nSources and further reading\nAndrej Karpathy on vibe coding (original post, Feb 2025): https://x.com/karpathy/status/1886192184808149383\nIBM, "What is vibe coding?": https://www.ibm.com/think/topics/vibe-coding\nSimon Willison, "Not all AI-assisted programming is vibe coding": https://simonwillison.net/2025/Mar/19/vibe-coding/\nWikipedia, Vibe coding: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibe_coding\nLovable documentation: https://docs.lovable.dev/\nCursor: https://www.cursor.com/\nAnthropic Claude Code: https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code'
WHERE title = 'What is Vibe Coding? A Guide for AI-First Builders'
  AND type = 'guidebook';